`Task.pm:64-71` — BUILD deletes optional fields only when `!defined`, so a
defined-but-falsy value counts as "set". Consumers then treat it as truthy state
(`Cmd/Pick.pm:108`/`:112`, `Cmd/List.pm:136`).

    # task with  blocked: false   (i.e. explicitly NOT blocked)
    karr list           -> "#1  backlog  Unblocked explicitly [medium, blocked]"
    karr pick --claim x -> "No available tasks to pick."   rc=0

    # task with  claimed_by: ""
    karr show 1         -> "Claimed:  "      (empty)
    karr pick --claim x -> "No available tasks to pick."   rc=0

`blocked: false` is exactly what kanban-md writes, so this triggers on any
imported board. The task silently disappears from the agent workflow — `pick`
reports "nothing to do" while a perfectly available task sits there.

Applies to every optional field with a defined falsy value: `assignee: ''`,
`estimate: 0`, `parent: 0`.

Fix: distinguish "absent" from "falsy" — check definedness and emptiness
explicitly at the consumer sites, and stop treating `0`/`''`/`false` as set.
Re-verified against main at 3dac607 (93 files / 630 tests green) with a sharper
reproduction than the ticket had. This is an interop showstopper, not a corner
case -- raising to critical.

A kanban-md-written card:

    ---
    id: 1
    title: kanban-written
    status: backlog
    priority: high
    blocked: false
    block_reason: ""
    claimed_by: ""
    ---

imported with `karr import --yes`, is stored with block_reason and claimed_by as
empty strings (blocked: false is dropped correctly by the #58/#69 work, the two
empty strings are not), and then:

    $ karr pick --claim bob
    No available tasks to pick.

on a board whose only task is unblocked, unclaimed and high priority. So after
importing a kanban-md board, karr pick is blind to all of it -- which is the
whole point of the bridge.

karr itself no longer produces this shape (it omits the keys), so it only
arrives through import, which is exactly the path that matters. The fix belongs
in the one pickability predicate: Cmd/Pick.pm::_is_pickable (added by #86) --
treat empty string as absent for claimed_by and block_reason, the same way an
absent key is treated. Check Cmd/List.pm filtering for the same assumption.
